Zeo patch 0002 — verify trusted-header sign-ins with Google; take name + picture.

Target: Open WebUI v0.11.3 (ghcr.io/open-webui/open-webui:v0.11.3).
Applied by ai/openwebui/Dockerfile.openwebui with `patch -p1` from /app.

Adds env var WEBUI_AUTH_TRUSTED_ACCESS_TOKEN_HEADER (default empty = feature
off, upstream behaviour). When set alongside WEBUI_AUTH_TRUSTED_EMAIL_HEADER,
the trusted-header sign-in path:
  * refuses the request unless Google's tokeninfo confirms the forwarded
    access token is live, issued to GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID, and belongs to the
    asserted (verified) e-mail;
  * takes display name and profile picture from Google's userinfo, on account
    creation AND on every later sign-in (pre-existing accounts self-heal).

Files: backend/open_webui/env.py, backend/open_webui/routers/auths.py,
       backend/open_webui/utils/trusted_proxy.py (new).
See ai/openwebui/OPENWEBUI.md § Single sign-on and § Custom image.

